# Phase C + Task 31 full-phase validation — architect, 2026-07-14
# Owner-requested re-validation of all Phase C work and the Task 31 session
# ("let's make sure we got everything green passed and per architecture").
# Method: 3 parallel audit agents (frontend↔schema contract, resolvers↔
# migrations, process/evidence/i18n) + independent on-disk verification of
# every agent finding + full gate re-execution + live cloud readbacks.
# Nothing was accepted from any report (agent or human) without re-execution.

## Verdict

Phase C frontend work and the Task 31 closure were process-clean (rules 7/8
exemplary, i18n parity perfect, SHAs verify against git), but the validation
found REAL runtime defects concentrated in two places: (1) all four M2
mutations in m2.ts were still written against the stale/draft schema — the
dd605b0 round fixed M3/M4 only and m2.ts was outside its blast radius;
(2) four frontend GraphQL contract violations in the M2/M3/M4 views that
tsc and hermetic (client-mocked) tests structurally cannot catch. All fixed,
tested, deployed, and live-verified this round except one item deliberately
BLOCKED-ON-OWNER (getDocumentVersionDiff — see below).

